{
  "slug": "classification-predicate",
  "title": "Classification Predicate",
  "definition": "A [term:predicate] that places a referent into a class or category (a ∈ B). Unlike an [term:equative-predicate], which asserts identity between two individuals, a classification predicate asserts that the subject belongs to a type. The predicate NP is typically indefinite. Strategies across languages include bare juxtaposition, a [term:copula], a [term:denominal-strategy], and predicative marking.",
  "relatedTerms": ["equative-predicate", "copula", "verbless-clause", "denominal-strategy", "predicate"],
  "examples": [
